{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this admission. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been vomiting since this morning—just watery stuff, no blood. I haven’t been able to keep anything down since yesterday’s dinner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever, abdominal pain, or diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. It feels just like my last few episodes—nausea, then vomiting, and I can’t eat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds consistent with your gastroparesis. We’ll keep you NPO for now—nothing by mouth—so your stomach can rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Again? How long will I have to stay like that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just until we get your nausea under control. We’re starting IV fluids and giving you anti-nausea meds like Zofran and Ativan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ativan? That’s for anxiety, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:05:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but it also helps with nausea, especially in cases like yours where stress or anxiety can make symptoms worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess that makes sense. My blood pressure was high earlier—should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:07:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your systolic was 200 when you arrived, but it’s already coming down now that we’ve treated your nausea. High BP like that is common during flares—your body’s under stress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I don’t need a new blood pressure med?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:08:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. We’ll stick with your usual lisinopril. Once you’re feeling better, your PCP can reassess whether you need another medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:09:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t seen my PCP in a while. I should probably fix that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:09:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ve already reached out to them. It might help to find someone closer to home for regular follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds good. What about my diabetes? I didn’t take my insulin today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re getting insulin through the IV as needed, and we’re continuing your long-acting glargine at night. Your glucose was 186 this morning—well controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:11:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about ketoacidosis again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:12:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of that. Your anion gap is normal, so we’re not concerned about DKA this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. What about the chest X-ray they did?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:13:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It showed your port is in good position, and your lungs are clear. There’s a little atelectasis—common when you’re not moving much—but nothing serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2199-04-01 17:14:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2199-04-02 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2199-04-02 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I haven’t vomited since last night, and the nausea is much lighter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2199-04-02 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’re going to check your labs again and see if we can start you on clear liquids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2199-04-02 08:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have water or broth?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2199-04-02 08:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with small sips. If you tolerate that, we’ll advance to a soft diet tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2199-04-02 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds? I’m still on Ativan and Reglan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2199-04-02 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, both are continuing. Reglan helps your stomach empty, and Ativan keeps nausea and anxiety in check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2199-04-02 08:04:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on amitriptyline for nerve pain. Should I keep taking that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2199-04-02 08:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve continued it at night. It also helps with sleep and can reduce nausea over time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2199-04-02 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2199-04-03 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You did well on clear liquids. We’re upgrading you to a soft diet today—mashed potatoes, applesauce, things like that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2199-04-03 09:00:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s great! I’ve missed eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2199-04-03 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just take it slow. Small, frequent meals work better for gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2199-04-03 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember from last time. What about my blood work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2199-04-03 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hemoglobin dropped a bit—from 12 to 10.7—so we’re watching your iron levels. But no need for a transfusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2199-04-03 09:03:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had anemia before. Should I take iron again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2199-04-03 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll discuss that with your PCP. For now, focus on nutrition and recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had no vomiting, and your abdomen is soft and non-tender. We’d like to try a regular diet today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s awesome. Does this mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow. We want to make sure you can keep food down and that your blood pressure stays stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My BP’s been in the 140s. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Much better than 200. It’s in a safe range for discharge. Just keep following up to get it lower long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds when I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same as before: lisinopril, citalopram, amitriptyline, glargine insulin, Reglan, and Ativan as needed for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:04:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I saw something about tapering Ativan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—take 0.5 mg twice daily for two days, then once daily for two more days, then stop. This prevents withdrawal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I need to see my gastroenterologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2199-04-04 10:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, for ongoing management. This flare wasn’t due to infection or blockage—just your usual gastroparesis pattern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2199-04-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2199-04-05 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. I feel so much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2199-04-05 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. Remember: small meals, stay hydrated, take your meds as directed, and follow up with your doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2199-04-05 08:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2199-04-05 08:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we hope not to see you back here soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2199-04-01 16:49:00",
    "admission_end": "2199-04-05 12:27:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes and a history of gastroparesis was admitted for a flare of nausea and vomiting. She was kept NPO initially, given IV fluids, and treated with anti-nausea medications including Ativan and Zofran. Her blood pressure, which was elevated at admission, normalized as her nausea improved. She gradually advanced to a regular diet, remained asymptomatic, and was discharged home in stable condition. No new medications were added, but she was advised to taper her Ativan to avoid withdrawal. Follow-up was arranged with her PCP and gastroenterologist for ongoing management of hypertension and gastroparesis.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Persistent vomiting",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
